IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ita-types`
IMPORT `ita-rates`
IMPORT `ita-reliefs`
IMPORT `cpf-contributions`
IMPORT `cpf-wages-year`
IMPORT `sg-household`

-- Independent tests for the household encoding: cases 1 to 70 of independent-expectations.md.
-- Every expected number is from independent-expectations.md (frozen 2026-11-24T14:28:54Z, sha256 in independent-expectations.frozen.txt), worked from the Income Tax Act 1947
-- and the CPF Act 1953 before any encoding file was opened. None was edited after the encoding was read. A failing assertion is a finding.
-- Where the Act is silent (a FORK in the expectations file) the assertion accepts either reading; which one the encoding took is in INDEPENDENT-TEST-REPORT.md.
-- Case 70 cannot be expressed in the encoding inputs (see the report); the supplementary cases are in tests-independent-supplement.l4, not here.

§ `Independent fixtures`

`a month of pay` ow aw MEANS `My pay in one month` OF ow, aw

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `income tax of the household`

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`CPF of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `employee CPF of the household`

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`net of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST p THEN p's `net income of the household`

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`first adult carry of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST p THEN (p's `the first adult's position`)'s `parenthood rebate carried forward`

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`second adult carry of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
    WHEN JUST p THEN
        CONSIDER p's `the second adult's position`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 0 MINUS 1
        WHEN JUST q THEN q's `parenthood rebate carried forward`

GIVEN h IS A `Household`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not covered` IF
    CONSIDER `the household's position` h
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST p THEN FALSE

§ `Independent cases`

`ADULT1A` MEANS `Adult of the household` WITH
    `my year of birth` IS 1990
    `my month of birth` IS 6
    `my residence status for CPF` IS `a citizen of Singapore`
    `I am resident in Singapore for income tax` IS TRUE
    `my wages month by month` IS LIST (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0), (`a month of pay` 500 0)
    `my trade, business or profession income, after its deductions` IS 0
    `my rent and other property income, after its deductions` IS 0
    `my tax-exempt income` IS 0
    `I am a married woman, a divorcee or a widow` IS FALSE
    `I am totally blind or permanently and severely disabled` IS FALSE
    `my life insurance premiums, capped at 7% of the capital sum` IS 0
    `my SRS contributions` IS 0
    `my SRS contribution cap` IS 15300
    `my CPF cash top-ups for family, after grants and as capped` IS 0
    `my CPF cash top-ups for myself, after grants and as capped` IS 0
    `the prescribed deduction limit for family top-ups` IS 8000
    `the prescribed deduction limit for my own top-ups` IS 8000
    `my dependants` IS EMPTY
    `incapacitated siblings I maintain` IS 0
    `my national service status` IS `not an operationally ready national serviceman`
    `I am the wife or widow of an NSman and claim` IS FALSE
    `I am the parent of an NSman and claim` IS FALSE
    `the caregiver grandparent's income from work` IS NOTHING
    `my parenthood rebate brought forward` IS 0

`HH1` MEANS `Household` WITH
    `the income year` IS 2025
    `the first adult` IS `ADULT1A`
    `the second adult` IS NOTHING
    `the adults are married to each other and live together` IS FALSE
    `the children` IS EMPTY

